WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:04.980
First, you put everything
you can think of into box A.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.520
Then, you look and think about what is in there

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.360
and if you find any problems with something,
you move it into box B.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.700
What are you talking about?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.410
It's a way to figure out what you
find "right" that a friend taught me.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.040
There's something wrong about every single thing.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.870
You have to notice that first.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.210
After you learn both the good and bad sides,

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.240
you can decide on what you find truly right.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.630
Does that mean Kei isn't perfect either?

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.720
I think so. Of course not.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Do you think he never makes mistakes?

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.270
If so, that seems a bit like a tragedy.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.750
If he never makes mistakes,

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.140
the moment he makes one,
he'll stop being Asai Kei to you,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.270
which I find tragic.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.590
I wouldn't be able to live knowing that
I'm not allowed to make any mistakes.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.320
You look like you're about to cry, Haruki.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:05.770
I think I need to think more about certain things.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.450
I don't know the bad sides of Asai Kei yet.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.770
Me neither.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.640
Let's think about it for a bit.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:19.720
You know, even I understand this.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.050
I'm human too, after all.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:26.390
Sacrificing a cat to save a human
must be the right thing to do.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.710
I think I'll be going home.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.980
I'll stay here for a bit longer.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.560
I'll be back.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.400
Sure.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.450
Nonoh.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.620
It's not like we're stopping
the cat's time for eternity.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:49.630
Kei will eventually find a way to save
everyone without sacrificing a cat.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.130
Yeah, I know.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:05.860
Yes?

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.950
Are you with Nonoh?

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:08.930
Yes.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.390
I was just about to go home.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:12.440
Good job.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.300
By the way, I want to ask you one thing.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.490
What is it?

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.160
Souma Sumire collapsed.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.340
I want to help her.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.000
What's Souma Sumire's condition?

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.250
She's still asleep.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.830
I don't know anything more.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.000
Was she carried here at your request?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.420
I asked Urachi to do that, yes.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.170
You're quick to act.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.220
Did you know this would happen?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:40.930
No.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.180
But...

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.470
I had my suspicions.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:47.060
What are you going to do?

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.230
I'll help her, just as planned.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.230
I expected her to get hurt.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.480
That's why I have to save her, just as planned.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.650
Asai Kei, you're not that righteous.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.990
You're neither good nor pure.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.660
But I'm sure you are a hero.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.620
You may not be omnipotent like you wish to be.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.620
You may be weak and reality might be cruel,

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.330
but you are truly a hero
even if you don't seem like one.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.050
I'm just doing as I please.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.300
Asai.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.800
Putting in an effort for others
sure seems to please you.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.100
Where's Haruki?

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.760
Heading this way as we speak.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.850
She really will do anything for you.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.520
This time she's helping me on one condition.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.810
She's really kind.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.860
Demanding something in exchange means she
understands the responsibility you're giving her.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.160
It's always been like that—
I owe everything to her help.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.370
Eat some chocolate once
you're done with everything.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:46.830
Chocolate works wonders when you're tired.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.120
<b>CRISPY!
Chocolate works wonders when you're tired.</b>

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.080
<b>CRISPY!</b>

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.420
Hi, Haruki.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.880
Good evening, Kei.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.010
I think Sakagami will be here any minute now.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.430
I'm sorry for asking this of you.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.100
I don't think the condition you
gave me will be difficult with his help.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.260
Why do you want this, though?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:10.270
Because I want to understand you.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.730
If you really aren't perfect,
I want to learn about it and try to understand.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.900
I'm not perfect at all.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.110
But I don't know your bad sides.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:27.410
I think that until now,
I've never really tried to understand you.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:32.250
Somewhere deep in my heart,
I've been wishing for you to never change.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:38.880
Kei, I've been afraid that my love for you
was blinding me to who you really are.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.510
What's wrong, Kei?

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.380
This is the second time you've said you loved me.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.760
When was the first?

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:52.770
You're going to remember that day in a moment.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.270
Are you ready?

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.230
Yes, please.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.360
Let's start, then.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.500
<i>So these are Kei's memories...</i>

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.210
<i>How kind yet cruel they are...</i>

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:19.380
<i>How clever yet foolish he is...</i>

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.460
<i>How bold yet sensitive he is...</i>

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.970
<i>Asai Kei is very special to me.</i>

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.760
<i>This equilibrium he maintains is perfect.</i>

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.060
<i>It's so beautiful and peaceful.</i>

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.560
I'm pretty sure I love you.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.360
Are you happy?

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:43.860
I don't know.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.700
How was it?

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.040
I found one of the mistakes you made.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:02.920
Two years ago, when you kissed me
on the rooftop of the south school building,

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.670
I was actually happy.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.390
If that's the case,

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.890
I sure took the long, cowardly way around.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.690
I did the same.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.240
What's wrong, Sumire, dear?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.160
You look awfully sad.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.120
Say, Tyltyl.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.040
Will you listen to my request?

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.170
Of course. Whatever it may be.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:47.920
Then make me the same as you, Tyltyl.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:52.510
Make me able to do anything, like you can.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.190
Good morning, Kei.

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:01.770
Morning.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.520
It's been a while.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.860
Yes, it certainly has.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:09.530
I thought you'd be visiting me more.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.280
It takes a lot of effort to get here.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.490
I'll try to keep that in mind, though.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.330
I don't mind!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.750
But please do try to visit more.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:18.830
Sure.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.040
By the way, have you seen Souma Sumire?

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.090
Me? No.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:25.800
Tyltyl met with her, though.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.050
Are you saving her this time?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.010
Yeah.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.130
What are you, some kind of a hero?

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:35.550
No, I'm Souma Sumire's friend.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:39.270
Souma is the second most important person to me.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:44.020
In such a ranking, only first place matters.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:48.110
She's sitting alone in a corner precisely
because second place means nothing.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.110
That might be true.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.280
Are you going to make her first?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.740
I'm going to get her to make do with being second.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.950
You're so cruel.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.160
I am.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.500
I am cruel and selfish.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.460
She's here?

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.550
The rooftop of the south school
building, the tetrapods...

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.340
Both are important places,

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:15.430
but to the Souma from two years ago.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.680
Not the current one.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:22.480
Once we're done with everything,
let's have a Kit Kat together.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.400
Take a break with some chocolate

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.770
and plan to make some curry together.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.150
We'll make the best curry in the world.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.240
Yeah.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:35.570
_________________
October 23 (Mon)

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:37.030
Haruki, save.
_________________
October 23 (Mon)

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.450
Save.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.250
It's 7:15:20 PM.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.040
Let's go.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.060
Why are you here?

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.310
This is my apartment. Of course I'd come back.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.110
You didn't have to come all the way
to the dream world for that.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.910
I will be the one to define your happiness.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.160
I don't think I can save you.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.410
But you can save me.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.830
You can make me happy.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.000
Impossible.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.290
I've hurt you.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.750
That's only what you think.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.260
You've been a greater help to me than anyone else.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.010
I'm sure of it.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:41.220
The happiness you ensured for me is true happiness.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:45.140
I really am happy.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.480
Thank you.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.070
So please, keep helping me.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.490
I can keep being happy thanks to you.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.990
It's too bright.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.120
Kei.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.450
You're always the same.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.870
And that's so unbearably painful for me.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:21.800
I knew it. You're crying.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.310
Look at my future.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:29.520
In one month, in half a year, in a year...

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:33.440
Whenever I see you, you're smiling.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:34.690
Look at that future.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.650
Kei.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:40.740
If that's what you wish for,
I'm sure that's how it'll be.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.290
But I'm scared of such a future.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.330
Knowing that I can't have you for myself

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.210
and I keep smiling despite that
is such a scary thought.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:50.880
You know?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.170
But fine.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.090
If you accept my one condition,

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.970
I'll do whatever you say.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.260
What is it?

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:02.220
Play a game with me.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.560
If you win, I'll do what you say.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.600
And if you win?

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:10.690
If I win, let me decide your future for you.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.190
You'll become mine.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:17.230
And you'll live here in this dream world.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.780
We'll live here together

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:23.910
like two pebbles, never causing any trouble for anyone.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.660
Sure. What kind of game will we play?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:32.790
You haven't said my name even once since entering this room.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.800
I'm sure you're being considerate.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:37.760
But...

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:41.880
Please, Kei. Say my name.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:46.390
If you say it right, you win.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.400
Good evening, Haruki.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.650
Took you a while.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:57.860
October 23 — (Mon)

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.610
<i>Thirty minutes have passed...
October 23 — (Mon)</i>

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.700
Have you met with Kei?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.320
Yeah, we talked.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.530
Where is he now?

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:08.950
In my hands.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.960
What is that supposed to mean?

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.380
Kei made a promise with me.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:18.300
We played a game, and he'd become mine if he lost.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.760
And he did lose.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.930
That's why he's like this now.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.010
That's impossible.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.390
Why?

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.350
I'm practically the same as Tyltyl now.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.680
Turning him into a pebble is no big deal for me.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:32.890
Souma Sumire.

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:35.650
There is no way you'd wish for such a thing.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.860
If I really were Souma Sumire, no.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.570
That's so stupid!

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:46.200
If that pebble isn't Asai Kei,

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.830
there's no need to be panicking that much, is there?

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.460
Haruki Misora, that really is him.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.460
He can't see or hear anything,

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.840
but keeps thinking inside there.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.960
It's a pebble which possesses his consciousness.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.880
I'm telling you, give up.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:07.390
He's already mine.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.050
Souma Sumire.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:12.220
Please forgive me for not mincing words.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:16.150
To think Haruki Misora has become so human...

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.310
Two years is quite a long time.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.820
Whatever,

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.900
there's no need to be considerate of me.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:25.610
Then...

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.490
This is absolutely ridiculous.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.620
You can't claim Asai Kei as yours
just because you've done this.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:36.920
You let me into this room exactly
because you're perfectly aware of that!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.000
You're like a child throwing a tantrum.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.880
You cannot be satisfied with such an outcome,

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.670
so you're trying to truly claim
Asai Kei for yourself now, aren't you?

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:49.260
Basically, you've been waiting for me
to come and let you have him, no?

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.560
I see, that's such an effective method.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.680
I was always on his side,
I even threw my life away for him,

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.350
so if I got depressed after all that,

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.360
he wouldn't be himself if he left me alone.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:04.900
And if I turned him into a pebble,

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:09.070
there was no way you wouldn't
come to save him, Haruki Misora.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:12.120
You put him way above yourself,

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:16.290
so you're even able to leave
his side if it's for his sake.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.620
And if that's the case...

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:21.290
Give Asai Kei to me.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.840
Souma Sumire.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:25.130
Did you know?

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:29.380
I used to be able to use my ability by myself.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.350
I could until the summer two years ago.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.100
But after one of my resets

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.430
Souma Sumire died, even though she didn't before.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.520
And so Asai Kei was hurt.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.570
That's when I became unable
to use my ability on my own.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:47.190
I didn't want the same thing to happen again.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.990
He's the only one.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:53.330
He's the only person who remembers what happens
before resets, and I didn't want him to get hurt.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:15:01.170
No, I was scared that if I used my ability
on my own and failed, he'd hate me.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:04.670
Can you use your reset without him now?

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.130
I can.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.260
Rese—

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.640
I'm so sorry.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:25.730
You really do care only about him, don't you?

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:37.290
There's no way I could've
missed that future, could I?

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:42.580
There's no way you'd just give him to me
after spending two years with him, right?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:47.210
There's no way Kei wouldn't
see through such a plan, right?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:52.930
It's not like I can calculate
every single thing to go my way.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:56.560
It's not like I can help having
feelings like everyone else!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:58.890
I'm sorry.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.810
It's fine.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:05.150
There's no point if you can't be fooled.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:10.320
So I was right that you
